<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p>Take Nairobi to be at (<m>1^\circ\,17'\,\mathrm{S}, 36^\circ\,49'\,\mathrm{E}</m>) and Mandera to be at (<m>3^\circ\,56'\,\mathrm{N}, 41^\circ\,52'\,\mathrm{E}</m>).</p><p>(a) Find the difference in latitude.</p><p><fillin characters="4" name="ans1"/> <m>^\circ</m> <fillin characters="4" name="ans2"/> <m>{}'</m>   </p><p>(b) Find the difference in longitude (the smaller angle between their meridians).</p><p><fillin characters="4" name="ans3"/> <m>^\circ</m> <fillin characters="4" name="ans4"/> <m>{}'</m>   </p></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>(a) Nairobi and Mandera are on opposite sides of the equator, so add the latitudes.</p><p><me>{1}^\circ\,{17}' + {3}^\circ\,{56}' = {5}^\circ\,{13}'</me></p><p>(b) Nairobi and Mandera are on the same side of the Greenwich meridian, so subtract the longitudes.</p><p><me>{41}^\circ\,{52}' - {36}^\circ\,{49}' = {5}^\circ\,0{3}'</me></p></p></solution>
    <answer><p><m>5</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>13</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>5</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>3</m></p></answer>
</stack-static>